<title>USA: Int'l Semiconductor unit furloughs staff.</title>
<headline>Int'l Semiconductor unit furloughs staff.</headline>
<dateline>LONG BEACH, Calif. 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Semiconductor Inc's GAD Semiconductors unit said it has furloughed most of its employees at Migdal H'amek industrial park in Israel after determining the overhead to manufacture gallium arsenide diodes there was too high.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said the number of employees furloughed was not immediately available.  International Semiconductor said it is negotiating with a U.S. electronics manufacturer to produce products using International Semi's technology.</p>
<p>Pending definitive resolution of the U.S. efforts, no further expenses will be incurred in Israel, it said.</p>
</text>
